From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: android-kitkat-tls12 <android-kitkat-tls12@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/30] Port of 2d089e18: stop depending on CipherSuite in
 OpenSSL-backed sockets

Port of external/conscrypt 2d089e18deae231149737cad6ce00f1e137a7199
("Stop depending on CipherSuite in OpenSSL-backed sockets", 5.0) onto the
KitKat libcore/crypto tree, with the matching libcore test change
bccd4e67d528d52d368e4bbd319621ba2cc15e5f ("No need to sanity-check client
certs in SSLSocket.accept") and the OpenSSLSocketImpl hunk of conscrypt
16c041fa20ef70221f487631f07eaf53d39ae51c ("Make some methods public for
CTS": getClientKeyType() is public, because conscrypt-tests and conscrypt
live in different class loaders on the device and in host Dalvik, and a
package-private call from NativeCryptoTest throws IllegalAccessError).

Why: the server side of OpenSSLSocketImpl and OpenSSLServerSocketImpl
looked up every enabled suite with CipherSuite.getByName(), which knows
only the Harmony SSLEngine suites. Once the TLS 1.2 rows (336e8eb) are
supported, a server socket with any *_SHA256/*_SHA384 suite enabled threw
a NullPointerException. The server key types now come from the SSL_CIPHER
list of the SSL itself (SSL_get_ciphers, algorithm_mkey/algorithm_auth).

KitKat differences:
- the 4.4 checkEnabledCipherSuites() used checkForPrivateKey(keyType,
  Class) and already skipped TLS_FALLBACK_SCSV (6c9609af5f); removed as
  upstream did;
- the JNI functions return early when to_SSL/to_SSL_CIPHER threw (NULL);
- NativeCrypto mode/option constants are unchanged; the new SSL_k*/SSL_a*
  values equal ssl/ssl_locl.h and TLS_CT_* equal ssl/tls1.h of our
  OpenSSL 1.0.1e (checked by check_tls_lists.py ssl-cipher-constants).

Android 4.3 port (android-4.3_r3) of patch 0002 of the 4.4 series. Paths
and names: libcore/crypto of 4.4 (org.conscrypt,
org_conscrypt_NativeCrypto.cpp in libjavacrypto) is libcore/luni on 4.3
(org.apache.harmony.xnet.provider.jsse,
org_apache_harmony_xnet_provider_jsse_NativeCrypto.cpp in libjavacore).
OpenSSLServerSocketImpl: 4.3 declares checkForPrivateKey(String, Class)
with a raw Class; the removal follows the 4.3 text. OpenSSLSocketImpl:
the old server key setup is removed at its 4.3 place (no ALPN on 4.3, so
the context differs) and the key type helpers go to the 4.3 end of the
class. The JNI part applies as is: 4.3 already passes SSL pointers as
jlong. The SSL_k*/SSL_a*/TLS_CT_* values are checked against the OpenSSL
1.0.1u headers of the 4.3 tree (patches/jb/4.3/external_openssl).
